#
# holt — Zig for a ctags that does not have it.
#
# Loaded ONLY after holt has MEASURED that this toolchain cannot extract Zig symbols, and
# defined under a PRIVATE name. Both matter, and the reason is not hypothetical: this definition
# used to live in the always-loaded pack under the real name `Zig`, and the moment upstream
# ctags gained its own Zig parser the load became FATAL — "Language \"Zig\" already
# defined", ctags exits, and holt gets ZERO symbols from EVERY file in the repository. Silence,
# which reads as "these agents share nothing".
#
# A private name cannot collide with a builtin. The measurement gate means a real builtin parser
# is never replaced by these regexes when one exists.
#
### Zig ########################################################################
--langdef=HoltZig
--map-HoltZig=+.zig
--kinddef-HoltZig=f,function,functions
--kinddef-HoltZig=c,class,structs and enums
--kinddef-HoltZig=v,variable,constants
--regex-HoltZig=/^[ \t]*(pub[ \t]+)?(export[ \t]+)?(inline[ \t]+)?fn[ \t]+([a-zA-Z_][a-zA-Z0-9_]*)/\4/f/
--regex-HoltZig=/^[ \t]*(pub[ \t]+)?const[ \t]+([a-zA-Z_][a-zA-Z0-9_]*)[ \t]*=[ \t]*(extern[ \t]+|packed[ \t]+)?(struct|enum|union|opaque)/\2/c/
--regex-HoltZig=/^[ \t]*(pub[ \t]+)?(const|var)[ \t]+([a-zA-Z_][a-zA-Z0-9_]*)[ \t]*[:=]/\3/v/
